A||||25||sloth85GT||How much Nitrous can it take?||||1||
Z||000000||sloth85GT||11-11-2001||05:57 PM||||I was wondering, since I'm planning on tossing in a 350 in my GT later, I was gonna have some extreme fun with my 2.8. How much nitrous can my stock 2.8 with 198,750km (119250 miles) take before blowing something up? I was thinking maybe a 100HP or a 125HP shot. What do you experts think?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.mts.net/~kuzma/fieronl.gif">     <BR>Dan<BR>1985 Silver GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-11-2001||06:12 PM||||just about this much....... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(jk,hehe)||||reg||7
Z||000002||fropuff||11-11-2001||06:28 PM||||Well, I'd say that 100 is the absolute maximum.  125, and your engine is pretty much out.  That's almost 100% of the original HP.  Most people with 2.8s are going 70-90.  I, myself, am planning to start with a 50 and build from there.  You also need to make sure that your engine's up for it.  Good fuel pressure, oil pressure, clean injectors, good fuel pump, good ignition, etc.  There's more than just slapping it on.  This is most of the time; 1FST2M6s is a different story!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Keep us posted. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||11-11-2001||08:17 PM||||Dude, find out for us!  (looking around for some carbon/kevlar-backed seats...)<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||sloth85GT||11-11-2001||09:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>Dude, find out for us!  (looking around for some carbon/kevlar-backed seats...)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The whole explosion thing didn't occur to me until Mach10 started scaring the crap outta me about how rods and stuff will fly right through the firewall. And fires too, I don't want any fires. If my engine blows, so be it, like I care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I just don't want anything to happen to the rest of my car. I wanna hear 1fst2m6's take on this one. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||11-11-2001||09:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sloth85GT:<BR><B> The whole explosion thing didn't occur to me until Mach10 started scaring the crap outta me about how rods and stuff will fly right through the firewall. And fires too, I don't want any fires. If my engine blows, so be it, like I care   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> I just don't want anything to happen to the rest of my car. I wanna hear 1fst2m6's take on this one. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HAHAHAHA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>I told him the story my shop teacher told me, about his buddies Camaro back in the 70s. Halfway through the 1/4, the motor broke the cam. Tore through the block, and up through the hood. They found it like 200M away, at the bottom of a 4ft crater  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Don't think that'll happen with this v6  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>I'd be more worried of blowing the motor, and starting an engine fire... But that's just me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||10
Z||000006||Standard||11-11-2001||09:38 PM||||Just get a nice sheet of 1/4" steel and mount it to the firewall.  Then go find out  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000007||MR2KLR||11-11-2001||09:51 PM||||When you do blow your motor if you throw a rod through the block the hot oil that will spray all over the engine bay WILL light off of the hotter than normal exhaust system. alot more damage that you may be ready to deal with. But other than that i'd say a 150 shot would kill her right, but you got alot of miles so a few 100 shots will do it. I learnd from puting NOS on a duke if you use a wet kit, dump abit more NOS than Gas and It will hit ALOT harder like motor mount snaping, Block spliting hard. and more gas than NOS and you will get more tourque||||reg||1
