Z||000012||1FST2M6||11-12-2001||09:32 AM||||how will you know if you blow your engine.. oh belive me you'll know..  if youv'e ever witnessed or been in an auto accident when the rod come through the side of the block and takes out the fender well and front suspension you'll know.. (my first nitrous car.. 79 Corvette KB pistons didnt' agree with the nitrous and took out all the parts in the passengerside of the engien bay)<P>how much can you spray... spray untill a catastrophic failure rebuild then down one jet.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i've got a 125.4 shot. and have since May(01) 14 bottles worth.   <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com/FIERO" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com/FIERO</A>   <BR> <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>  20920 is the part number... running a  62 n2o and a 24 fuel, with 19#/hr injectors, camaro fuel pump and 2.5" exhaust. the better your exhaust works the better your N2O kit will work. ||||reg||1
Z||000013||cardealer||11-12-2001||04:14 PM||||depends on what type of system it is and where it is injected. one question, "why do it?" <BR>the possiblities of additional damage to your tranny, and other componets could force you in sending more money on your v8 conversion, besides as long as your stock fiero engine can be rebuilt it is worth something to someone. when i did my v8 conversion my v6 was had 110,000 miles on it and it ran great, i sold it for $200.00.<BR>just some thoughts.||||reg||1
